to reform things instead of  trying to improve their position by  raising wages the Communists say that  the proletariat has to take power  political power take over the state and  therefore take over the means of  production as well this leads us to  another key idea of the Communists one  of the ones that's probably the most  controversial which is that private  property as we know it as we understand  it in terms of bourgeois private  property needs to be abolished and  replaced by social property or  state-owned property there's a lot to be  said about this but we'll talk about  that more in some of the other videos  finally one of the other key themes is  that of what we call ideology and  ideology is a set of ideas so it's a  it's a connected set of ideas a loggia  logos of those  that represents the perspective or the  interests of a particular class at a  particular time but it's viewed by them  as being universal eternal good for all  human beings and so there's a kind of  masking that's going on of the real  situation etiology purports to tell us  the way things really are but it  actually conceals the way things truly  are and it ends up reflecting a kind of  false consciousness and it's very  difficult to combat but that's part of  what the Marxists are attempting to do  is to critique ideology so those are the  key themes to keep in mind as we go  through this work one last thing that I  would say particularly with this guy  there's a lot of historical baggage  associated with Marx and so if you  approach it saying I don't want to learn  anything cuz I know this guy's just a  dirty communist or a socialist and those  guys are all bad they want to take away  everything including my toothbrush  you're probably not going to get much  out of reading the work this is one of  those cases where you you probably want  to put aside whatever preconceived ideas  you have so you can read the text and  see what the text is actually saying and  then if you find yourself disagreeing  with the text afterwards after you fully  understood it that's perfectly fine
 

